        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Rare Opportunity to Own a Piece of Meath`s Heritage. \n\nDating from c.1790, this exceptional four bedroom period residence occupies a prime position in the heart of the historic heritage town of Kells. Extending over three levels and included on the National Inventory of Architectural Heritage, this is a truly unique opportunity to acquire a home of outstanding architectural and historical significance.\n\nPainted in striking traditional colours, the property immediately commands attention on one of Kells` most prominent streets. Its impressive faade showcases many of its original architectural details, including a pitched tiled roof with rendered chimney stacks, rendered walls with quoins, timber sash windows with moulded surrounds and stone sills and an elegant round-arched entrance framed by flanking Ionic columns. A delicate petal-pattern wrought iron fanlight, timber panelled front door and stone steps create a grand first impression, while wrought iron railings set on a limestone plinth wall enhance the property`s timeless character.\nInside, the home is rich in original period features that have been carefully preserved, reflecting the craftsmanship of a bygone era. Elegant reception rooms boast ornate cornicing, picture rails, decorative ceiling roses and magnificent fireplaces, including a beautiful Kilkenny marble fireplace. A striking spiral staircase provides a stunning architectural focal point, while arched windows and other original details further enhance the home`s distinctive character. The traditional AGA adds warmth and authenticity to the kitchen, blending seamlessly with the property`s historic charm.\nBeyond the house, the private cobblelock rear garden provides a peaceful retreat in the centre of town. A terraced seating area, mature rockery and a beautiful established plum tree create an inviting outdoor setting, while traditional stone walls and a gateway to the rear laneway add both character and convenience. The property also benefits from valuable off-street private parking for one car.\n\nCombining rich history, exceptional architectural features and an enviable town-centre location, this is a landmark home that offers the rare chance to become the custodian of an important piece of Meath`s heritage while enjoying all the amenities Kells has to offer.\n\nAccommodation: GROUND FLOOR - Entrance Hallway, Sitting Room, Study, Dining Room, Bedroom 1. BASEMENT - Kitchen, Dining Room, Utility Room, Shower Room, Landing with Store. FIRST FLOOR - Master Bedroom, Ensuite, Bedroom 2, Bedroom 3, Bathroom, Landing with hotpress. Floor Space c. 172 sq.m.\n\nLOCATION\nIdeally positioned in the heart of Kells, the property enjoys easy access to the M3 motorway, providing an excellent commuter link to Dublin and beyond.\n\nKells is one of Ireland`s most historic and vibrant heritage towns, offering an exceptional quality of life with an excellent range of amenities. \nA selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools are all within walking distance, making the location ideal for families.\n\nThe town boasts an excellent choice of sporting facilities, including the renowned Headfort Golf Club, swimming pool, GAA, soccer and rugby clubs, together with a wide variety of shops, cafs, award-winning restaurants, traditional pubs and hotels. \nKells is also home to a thriving community and a rich cultural calendar, hosting events such as the acclaimed Hinterland Festival of Literature Arts and the Samhain Festival of Food Culture, both of which attract visitors from across the country.\n\nSteeped in history yet offering every modern convenience, Kells provides the perfect setting to enjoy the unique character of this exceptional period home.\n\nGround Floor - Entrance Hallway\nImpressive entrance hallway featuring parquet flooring, ornate cornicing and a centre ceiling rose. A striking spiral staircase, with feature arch window, creates a stunning focal point.\n\nGround Floor - Sitting Room\nFront-facing reception room featuring original cornicing, a picture rail, an ornate ceiling rose and decorative curtain pelmets. Tastefully decorated and carpeted, the room is centred around a Kilkenny marble fireplace with an open fire, creating an elegant focal point. A feature columned archway leads through to the study.\n\nGround Floor - Study\nLeading from the Sitting Room and overlooking the back garden.\n\nGround Floor - Dining Room\nElegant front-facing formal dining room featuring original cornicing, a picture rail, an ornate ceiling rose and decorative curtain pelmets. An ornate fireplace with original tiled inlays forms a beautiful focal point, showcasing the home`s rich period character.\n\nGround Floor - Bedroom 1\nTo the rear and overlooking the back garden. Carpeted.\n\nBasement - Kitchen\nTiled kitchen with large oil fired AGA and quaint features such as a traditional pullymaid for drying clothes.\n\nBasement - Dining Room\nCosy `everyday` dining room with open fireplace.\n\nBasement - Utility Room\nTiled and plumbed. Storage.\n\nBasement - Shower Room\nMains shower, w.h.b., w.c. and storage unit. Tiled flooring.\n\nFirst Floor - Master Bedroom\nSpacious front-facing master bedroom, carpeted and featuring fitted wardrobes. Two sash windows fill the room with natural light. Access to ensuite.\n\nFirst Floor - Ensuite\nFully tiled. Electric power shower, w.h.b, W.C.\n\nFirst Floor - Bedroom 2\nTo the front. Carpeted and featuring fitted wardrobes.\n\nFirst Floor - Bedroom 3\nTo the rear. Access to hotpress.\n\nFirst Floor - Bathroom\nSpacious bathroom with W.C., bath and w.h.b.\n\nOutside\nPrivate cobblelock rear garden featuring a terraced seating area, rockery with mature planting and a beautiful mature tree, creating a peaceful outdoor space. Traditional stone walls add to the character, with a gateway providing access to the rear laneway. Off-street private parking is available for one car at the rear. Gated lane private access (Leather Alley/Lane).\n\nDirections\nJohn Street, Kells. Follow eircode A82 R827.\n\nwhat3words /// tobacco.worms.protrude\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
